---
description: Production schedule and stage ordering
alwaysApply: true
---

All scheduling must use America/New_York slate logic.

Implement this UTC schedule in .github/workflows/nba_pmf_delivery.yml:

06:30 UTC:
- after_game
- scores previous ET slate

07:30 UTC:
- model_chain (primary promote run, 3:30 AM ET)
- settled-stat refresh
- nightly training/calibration
- Phase 8 (~3.5 h) + Phase 13 (~2.5 h) = done by ~13:30 UTC (9:30 AM ET)
- promotion allowed only if gates pass
- starts ~1 h after after-game scoring so game data is fully settled

12:30 UTC:
- model_chain backup retry
- promotion allowed only if gates pass (catches 07:30 UTC failures)

14:00 UTC:
- predict current ET slate
- by this time promotion is already complete (model trained through prev day)

14:30 UTC:
- promotion cutoff
- after this, same-day promotion is forbidden

15:00 UTC:
- WoO morning delivery

15:30 UTC:
- model_chain_no_promote

18:00 UTC:
- WoO afternoon refresh

18:30 UTC:
- model_chain_no_promote

20:00 UTC:
- WoO late refresh

21:30 UTC:
- model_chain_no_promote

22:25 UTC through 03:25 UTC:
- Derek candidate windows
- slate-aware valid-skip outside useful pre-tip windows

For an 8:30 PM ET game:
- 23:55 UTC same day => derek_near_lineup
- 00:10 UTC next day => derek_near_lineup
- 00:25 UTC next day => close_lock
- 06:30 UTC next day => after_game for that slate

Training/Phase jobs must never block WoO/Derek delivery.
Remove workflow-level concurrency. Use job-level concurrency.
